From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artyom Shalkhakov <artyom.shalkhakov@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0500
Subject: [PATCH] Own the alert panel through the _window ivar, not an association

Dismissing an alert can crash with a use-after-free at the next
autorelease-pool drain.

The panel is stored into NSAlert's _window ivar with object_setIvar,
which retains nothing, and the only strong reference to it is an
associated object installed with OBJC_ASSOCIATION_RETAIN_NONATOMIC.
GNUstep's own NSAlert assumes the opposite: its -_setupPanel stores the
alloc'd panel into the MRC _window ivar at +1, and every consumer
balances exactly that one reference -- -runModal and both
-beginSheetModalForWindow:... variants call DESTROY(_window), and
-dealloc calls RELEASE(_window). With _window left unowned, the
un-swizzled sheet path's DESTROY(_window) over-releases the panel, and
the association cleanup when the NSAlert itself deallocates then
releases memory that has already been freed.

Honour that ownership contract instead. This file is compiled with ARC,
so hand the ivar a real +1 via a bridged retain and keep no associated
strong reference on top of it. The deferred cleanup -- which runs 0.1s
after the modal session ended, by which time the window system has no
pending operations on the panel, it is ordered out, and its delegate
and default-button cell are cleared -- consumes that +1 by transferring
the reference into an ARC temporary that releases at end of scope. On
the sheet paths _window is already nil, because GNUstep's own DESTROY
consumed the +1 there, so that block is skipped and nothing is released
twice.
---
diff --git a/NSAlert+Eau.m b/NSAlert+Eau.m
index 279b338..c83ada4 100644
--- a/NSAlert+Eau.m
+++ b/NSAlert+Eau.m
@@ -1577,20 +1577,22 @@ static void setKeyEquivalent(NSButton *button)
                 // NSLog(@"Eau: Exception during window cleanup: %@", e);
             }
 
-            // NSLog(@"Eau: Clearing _window ivar on NSAlert (keeping associated object to prevent premature dealloc)");
+            // Consume the +1 that eau_setupPanel stored in the ivar (the
+            // same reference GNUstep's DESTROY(_window)/RELEASE(_window)
+            // would consume on the paths that reach them). This runs from a
+            // deferred perform (0.1s after the modal ended), so the window
+            // system has no pending operations on the panel any more — the
+            // panel is ordered out, delegate and default-button cell
+            // cleared. On the sheet paths _window is already nil (GNUstep's
+            // own DESTROY consumed the +1 there), so this block is skipped
+            // and nothing is released twice.
             object_setIvar(self, windowIvar, nil);
-            // IMPORTANT: Do NOT release the associated object here.  The _window ivar
-            // in GNUstep's NSAlert is __weak, so the associated object with
-            // OBJC_ASSOCIATION_RETAIN_NONATOMIC is the ONLY strong reference keeping
-            // the EauAlertPanel alive.  Releasing it here triggers -dealloc while the
-            // window system (DPS/X11 backend) may still have pending operations or
-            // references to the panel, causing a crash (segfault) after dealloc
-            // completes.  The associated object will be automatically released when
-            // NSAlert itself is deallocated, which is a safe time for the panel to die.
-            //
-            // The panel is fully inert at this point (no delegate, no animation, ordered
-            // out) so keeping it alive until NSAlert deallocates is safe and prevents
-            // the use-after-free crash.
+            {
+                // Balance the +1 without any CF dependency: transfer it into
+                // an ARC temporary, which releases at end of scope.
+                id consumed = (__bridge_transfer id)(__bridge void *)currentWindow;
+                (void)consumed;
+            }
         }
     }
     else
@@ -1739,8 +1741,20 @@ static void setKeyEquivalent(NSButton *button)
         Ivar windowIvar = class_getInstanceVariable([self class], "_window");
         if (windowIvar)
         {
-            object_setIvar(self, windowIvar, panel);
-            objc_setAssociatedObject(self, kEAUAlertWindowRetainKey, panel, OBJC_ASSOCIATION_RETAIN_NONATOMIC);
+            // OWNERSHIP CONTRACT: GNUstep's own -_setupPanel stores the
+            // alloc'd panel into the MRC _window ivar at +1, and every
+            // consumer balances exactly that one reference — -runModal and
+            // both -beginSheetModalForWindow:… variants call
+            // DESTROY(_window), and -dealloc calls RELEASE(_window).
+            // This file is compiled with ARC, so hand the ivar a real +1
+            // via CFBridgingRetain. Do NOT keep an associated strong
+            // reference on top: the previous associated-object scheme left
+            // _window unowned, so the (un-swizzled) sheet path's
+            // DESTROY(_window) over-released the panel, and the association
+            // cleanup at NSAlert dealloc then released the already-freed
+            // panel — a use-after-free crash at the next autorelease-pool
+            // drain.
+            object_setIvar(self, windowIvar, (__bridge id)(__bridge_retained void *)panel);
             // NSLog(@"Eau: Successfully set _window via ivar");
         }
         else
